From a6fe57744e24c1833ee233a7f388bd04f682f53d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Craterbrain <58347640+Craterbrain@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 07:37:34 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] PlaitOS: Files and the file picker restyled after the FX
 mock-up
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- Material 3 Files UI switched on (force_material3): it was built in but
  off, so the legacy layouts were showing
- One top bar for Files and every picker mode: Home › storage › folders
  path (tappable), Up arrow, Close on a picker's Places; replaces the
  title, the drawer's hamburger and the second breadcrumb row; the
  picker's caller as a line under the path
- Places (Home) for Files and pickers: storage card, places, providers,
  other apps; pickers open on Places; Back from a storage root returns
  there; Places sits below the bar
- Folders and files as tiles (56 dp tonal / neutral squares, name in two
  lines, check badge, no ring), four columns, grouped by kind in every
  activity; list rows on the same tiles; design-guide type icons
- Type chips and the other-apps strip off while browsing; no column
  header on phones; Grid/List in More; folder-only items hidden on Places
- Browsing tabs, Open with sheet, selection/paste/picker footers (Compose,
  from the earlier Codex pass) kept and applied to all activities

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017VXjYUWzBqMCeUoJD2Suc4
